# soc_tb Linux smoke on the vec-serial RTL, 2026-10-15 (sw/linux/README.md recipe;
# OpenSBI v1.9 cbf9f67 and Linux 6.6 defconfig + embedded /init, both rebuilt today).
# Result: SOC TB TIMEOUT after 1,000,000,000 cycles (wall 7,163 s). The kernel boots and
# /init prints its uname line, then the hart livelocks in S-external interrupts (PLIC/UART):
# ~344k S-ext IRQ traps after ~500M cycles; PCs sampled every 5M cycles from 450M to 645M
# are all in do_irq / plic_handle_irq / handle_riscv_irq / _save_context.
# An instrumented soc_tb (probes of vec_start and vls_is via --public-flat-rw) counted ZERO
# vector-unit starts and ZERO vector load/store cycles through 550M cycles: the reworked
# vector logic never activates in this workload, and with it idle the scalar pipeline is
# the same as origin/main. The M-level trap trace is cycle-identical to origin/main RTL
# over the first 12M cycles. Linux had not been re-run since misa.V landed (stage 8).
# origin/main RTL (vector unit + VRF stubbed for simulation speed; the TB aborts if a vector
# instruction reaches EX, none did) reaches uname at ~500M cycles and livelocks identically:
# all 37 fetch-PA/data-address samples (every 5M cycles, 450M..630M) match this branch exactly.

VECCOUNT cy=0 starts=0 vls_cycles=0
VECCOUNT cy=50000000 starts=0 vls_cycles=0
VECCOUNT cy=100000000 starts=0 vls_cycles=0
VECCOUNT cy=150000000 starts=0 vls_cycles=0
